No permission is granted to use, copy, modify, distribute, or run it.

That restriction is not about the code. It is about where the code points.

This is a scraper, and it fetches from a real website run by real people who
never asked to be scraped. It tries hard to be a good guest: one request at a
time behind a single shared gate, a courtesy delay that shrinks slowly and
backs off hard at the first sign of strain, a contact address in the
User-Agent of every request, and a full stop when the site says to slow down.

None of that survives being copied. A hundred individually polite clients
arriving at once is not a hundred polite visitors — it is an outage, and the
people who would deal with it are not the ones who chose to run the copies.

So please read it, take the ideas, and ask me anything about it. Just don't
point another copy of it at their servers.
